UNBOUNDED FINITE-PARAMETER IDENTITIES
m=d*k, k>0; n=m*e-epsilon; epsilon=+/-1; r arbitrary; hence gcd(m,n)=1.
alpha=epsilon*e, eta=-epsilon, alpha*m+eta*n=1.
C1=(bn/q,m/q,0), C2=(-br,0,m), C3=(0,r,n).
K0=alpha*C2+eta*C3=(-alpha*b*r,eta*r,1).
C2-m*K0=-eta*q*r*C1; C3-n*K0=alpha*q*r*C1.
D=-b*e*s implies L=b*r*(alpha+eta*e)*s=0; remaining relation=-3*epsilon*s.
Affine power: t -> t+(I-T)h; norm map v -> v+N_m lambda; inverses use -h and -lambda.
